abstract: >-
  The World Engine is a computational framework for discovery systems that
  model behavior as a probabilistic emission from an evolving, partially
  observed state. It organizes shared behavioral dynamics as Archetypes,
  instantiates transition hypotheses called Digital Minds, detects emerging
  multivariate patterns through Signal Intelligence, and evaluates candidates
  by simulating possible state transitions.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - predictive discovery
  - recommender systems
  - behavioral computing
  - latent behavioral dynamics
  - world models
  - signal intelligence
  - digital minds
  - state-space models
